          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em lax natural transformation
            is a generalization of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %p
            As a natural transformation is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            between two
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functors"} 2-functors
            between
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
          %p
            Where a natural transformation has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+square"} commuting
            naturality square, a lax natural transformation has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
            filling that square. If that 2-morphism is required to be invertible, one speaks of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudonatural+transformation"} pseudonatural transformation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-natural+transformation"} strict 2-natural transformation
            (this latter notion only really makes sense for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-functors"} strict 2-functors
            between
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-categories"} strict 2-categories
          %p
            In the general terminology of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-transfor"} 1-transfor
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Given (possibly weak)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C,D
            and (possibly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+functor"} lax
            or oplax)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functors"} 2-functors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F, G : C\to D
            %strong lax natural transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha:F\Rightarrow G
            is given by
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in C
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphism"} 1-morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
